 can be passed by the Legislature to protect Texans.</quote><stance>-2</stance><direction>steady</direction><topic>moratorium</topic><src>Texas Tribune</src><url>https://www.texastribune.org/2026/11/04/data-center-texas-pause-gina-hinojosa-governor-policies/</url><prec>exact</prec></row><row i="12"><date>2026-10-21</date><who>Dan Patrick</who><office>Lt. Governor (outgoing Jan 2027)</office><st>TX</st><party>R</party><type>direct quote</type><quote>As I've told the data center industry, this is your Bud Light moment. You've really messed up.</quote><stance>-2</stance><direction>relaxing (less restrictive)</direction><topic>local consent / guardrails</topic><src>FOX34</src><url>https://www.fox34.com/2026/10/21/lt-gov-dan-patrick-campaigns-lubbock-says-state-must-regulate-data-centers/</url><prec>exact</prec></row><row i="13"><date>2026-10-20</date><who>Keisha Lance Bottoms</who><office>Governor-elect (takes office Jan 2027)</office><st>GA</st><party>D</party><type>direct quote</type><quote>Georgia is currently No. 1 in the country for data centers. We need to pause.</quote><stance>-2</stance><direction>steady</direction><topic>pause</topic><src>WTOC</src><url>https://www.wtoc.com/2026/10/20/bottoms-focuses-campaign-affordability-calls-data-center-pause/</url><prec>exact</prec></row><row i="14"><date>2026-10-12</date><who>Amy Acton</who><office>Governor-elect (takes office Jan 2027)</office><st>OH</st><party>D</party><type>direct quote</type><quote>I've called for a conditional moratorium very early in this campaign. We can't have companies coming in the dark of night. Communities deserve to know what businesses are coming to their community, and have a say in that.</quote><stance>-2</stance><direction>steady</direction><topic>transparency / conditional moratorium</topic><src>WVXU</src><url>https://www.wvxu.org/politics/2026-10-12/how-data-centers-impact-midterm-elections-ohio</url><prec>approximate (article/month)</prec></row><row i="15"><date>2026-09-30</date><who>A